<title>USA: Schnitzer, Proler to merge.</title>
<headline>Schnitzer, Proler to merge.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schnitzer Steel Industries Inc said it agreed to buy Proler International Corp through a cash tender offer, priced at $7.50 per share.</p>
<p>Upon completion of the tender offer, Proler will become a wholly owned Schnitzer unit. Proler has about 4.7 million shares outstanding, putting merger's value at $35 million.</p>
<p>Schnitzer's tender offer will be conditioned on at least a majority of Proler's outstanding shares being validly tendered and not withdrawn prior to expiration of the offer.</p>
<p>The expiration date will be twenty business days following the commencement, unless extended.</p>
</text>
